CPEDAL 1
NAME "BearFoot Blueberry Bass Overdrive Reference Draft"

# Reconstructed from the supplied verified Effects Layouts BearFoot BBOD board
# and cross-checked against Aion's Procyon V2 schematic/variant annotations.
# The supplied layout uses CA3130EZ, 2N5457, A250k Drive, A50k Tone and B50k
# Volume, so those values are retained even where BJFe-era units differ.
#
# The circuit uses several frequency-dependent feedback paths rather than a
# generic distortion block. Red LEDs provide the first soft-clipping limit,
# 1N4007s provide a later hard clamp, and a JFET buffers/drives the output.
#
# The original CA3130 external compensation capacitor is absorbed into the
# compact CA3130 dynamic model for now because the generic op-amp primitive
# does not expose the device's compensation pins.

V VRAW VRAW 0 9
R R_SUPPLY VRAW VA 51
C C_SUPPLY_1 VA 0 100n
C C_SUPPLY_2 VA 0 100u
C C_SUPPLY_3 VA 0 470n
AUDIO GUITAR INPUT 0 0.20

# Mid-supply reference. The Blueberry substitutions use equal 47k legs.
R R_VB_TOP VA VB 47k
R R_VB_BOTTOM VB 0 47k
C C_VB VB 0 22u

# Input coupling/bias.
R RPD INPUT 0 2M2
C C1 INPUT INPUT_BIAS 22n
R R1 VB INPUT_BIAS 360k
R R2 INPUT_BIAS OP_PLUS 14k7

# CA3130 voltage-amplifier stage.
OPAMP U1 OP_PLUS OP_MINUS OP_OUT VA 0 CA3130EZ

# Main soft-clipping feedback. Increasing DRIVE increases closed-loop gain.
D D1 OP_MINUS OP_OUT LED_RED
D D2 OP_OUT OP_MINUS LED_RED
R R3 OP_MINUS DRIVE_LOW 3k
POT DRIVE DRIVE_LOW OP_OUT OP_OUT 250k LOG 0.55

# Base low-frequency leg of the inverting network.
R R4 OP_MINUS LOW_FB 1k
C C3 LOW_FB 0 220n

# Post-op-amp dynamic hard clipping and stepped filtering.
R R5 OP_OUT POST_COUPLE 1k
C C7 POST_COUPLE CLAMP_A 1u
D D3 CLAMP_A 0 1N4007
D D4 0 CLAMP_A 1N4007

# First frequency-dependent feedback entry point.
C C8 CLAMP_A FB_A 22n
R R6 FB_A OP_MINUS 27k

# Low-pass step and second feedback entry point.
R R7 CLAMP_A CLAMP_B 10k
C C10 CLAMP_B 0 22n
C C9 CLAMP_B FB_B 4n7
R R8 FB_B OP_MINUS 147k

# JFET isolation/output stage. Aion Procyon V2 lists the drain resistor as
# R10 = 5k6; the Blueberry substitution list does not alter this value. The
# temporary 56k change made after the first physical test silenced this stage
# and was based on resistor numbering from an older schematic revision.
C C11 CLAMP_B Q1G 47n
R R9 Q1G 0 1M
JFET Q1 Q1D Q1G Q1S 2N5457
R R10 VA Q1D 5k6
R R11 Q1S 0 2k6

# The three-terminal Tone control is intentionally used with its wiper grounded.
# One end varies source bypass/bass reinforcement; the other varies the final
# high-cut. This preserves the unusual interactive control topology rather than
# reducing it to a single EQ filter.
R R12 Q1S TONE_BASS 2k
C C12 TONE_BASS TONE_1 22n
POT TONE TONE_1 0 TONE_3 50k LOG 0.50

# Drain output, Blueberry coupling/filter values, and level.
C C13 Q1D OUTPUT_PRE 1u
R R14 OUTPUT_PRE LEVEL_TOP 27k
C C15 LEVEL_TOP TONE_3 2n2
POT VOLUME 0 OUT LEVEL_TOP 50k LIN 0.55
R R_OUT_LOAD OUT 0 1M

OUTPUT OUT 0.5
